"program_narrative": "Program SECMGR is an online (CICS) security service invoked with SECURITY-REQUEST-AREA that performs one of three security functions per call. For a validate request (V) it obtains the signed-on CICS user ID with EXEC CICS ASSIGN and confirms it matches SEC-USER-ID. For an authorise request (A) it counts matching rows in DB2 table AUTHFILE for the user, resource and access type and grants access when the count is above zero. For an audit request (L) it collects the user, terminal and transaction IDs from CICS and inserts an access record into DB2 table AUDITLOG. Results are returned in SEC-RESPONSE-CODE (0 success, 8 validation failed or access denied, 12 technical failure) with a message in SEC-ERROR-INFO, and the program ends with EXEC CICS RETURN. Error conditions handled: CICS ASSIGN failure (12), user mismatch (8), SQL failure on the authorisation query (12), no authorisation row (8), and audit insert failure (12); an unrecognised request type performs nothing.",
"paragraphs": [
